System.Net.Security for witos (plan step W2.2, RFC 0015 section 8): the project targets the unix flavor when the build
is for witos, as System.Net.Http does, since HttpClient's unix flavor reaches System.Net.Security's types on every
request, plain HTTP too (the connection pool's application protocols), and the platform-neutral flavor throws
PlatformNotSupportedException from each of them. TLS goes through OpenSSL's shim and Negotiate through GSSAPI's, neither
of which the witos build makes until W3.1, so SslStream and NegotiateAuthentication fail explicitly when they are used.

--- a/src/libraries/System.Net.Security/src/System.Net.Security.csproj
+++ b/src/libraries/System.Net.Security/src/System.Net.Security.csproj
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
   <PropertyGroup>
     <TargetFrameworks>$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-windows;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-linux;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-freebsd;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-haiku;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-android;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-osx;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-ios;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-tvos;$(NetCoreAppCurrent)</TargetFrameworks>
+    <TargetFrameworks Condition="'$(TargetOS)' == 'witos'">$(TargetFrameworks);$(NetCoreAppCurrent)-unix</TargetFrameworks>
     <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
     <!-- This is needed so that code for TlsCipherSuite will have no namespace (causes compile errors) when used within T4 template  -->
     <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);PRODUCT</DefineConstants>
